figdown 0.3 block
# NEGATIVE (`DRAWN-ANNOTATION-FORM`): a DRAWN `note=` must survive a migration run
# COMPLETELY UNTOUCHED.
#
# The `note=`→`description=` rewrite was LINE-AGNOSTIC until this release.
# `note=` is live again language-wide as the drawn annotation, so left as it
# was the rule would have fired on every `node`, `group`, `edge` and `title`
# line in every downstream corpus and silently turned a box the author drew
# on purpose into a tooltip nobody can see — ink deleted, no diagnostic, by
# the one tool a user is asked to run unattended over their whole tree.
#
# Section 1 is the counter-example: four acceptors, four `note=` values, and
# the golden is this file BYTE FOR BYTE.
#
# Section 2 is the rule still doing its job, in the one scope where `note=`
# really is the retired tooltip key: a `field` line. Keeping both halves in
# ONE fixture is the point — a fixture that only showed survival would also
# pass against a tool that had deleted the rule outright, and fixture 206
# alone would pass against the line-agnostic version this replaces.
title "Drawn notes survive" note="a figure-level note, and title takes no other option key"
group fabric "Fabric" note="on a group"
node spine "Spine" in=fabric note="on a node — THIS is the line that used to be silently rewritten"
node leaf "Leaf" in=fabric
edge spine -> leaf note="on an edge"

figdown 0.1 bitfield
# Section 2: the surviving scope. `field` is the only directive that ever
# accepted `note=`, so this one IS the retired tooltip key and IS rewritten.
bitfield h "H" word=16 numbering=lsb0
field "A" 8 note="the low half"
field "B" 8
